# Architecture Plan: Issue #27 — Replace app background with a bold multi-color gradient

## Project shape
- Vite + React + TypeScript single-page static inbox prototype.
- Tailwind CSS is configured in `tailwind.config.js`; app-wide component styles are centralized in `src/styles/global.css` using Tailwind `@apply` plus CSS custom properties.
- There is no backend, database, auth layer, routing library, or runtime service dependency involved in this visual change.

## Module structure and file organization
- `src/main.tsx`: React entrypoint and global stylesheet import.
- `src/App.tsx`: Top-level app switch between inbox and reader views.
- `src/components/`: Reusable UI components such as `AppShell`, `MessageCard`, `ComposePanel`, and visual accent helpers.
- `src/views/`: Inbox and reader screen-level components.
- `src/store/`: Custom `useSyncExternalStore` interaction store and localStorage persistence.
- `src/types/` and `src/fixtures/`: Shared message types and seed inbox data.
- `src/styles/global.css`: Primary implementation target for Issue #27 because `.app-shell` currently owns the page background treatment.
- `src/styles/tokens.ts` and `src/styles/tokens.test.ts`: Token mirror and tests. Update only if the gradient requires new named token values or if the neutral base token itself changes.
- `index.html`: Update `theme-color` only if the chosen gradient has a clear dominant top/background color that should influence browser chrome.

## Issue dependency plan
- Only Issue #27 is in scope, so there are no cross-issue dependencies.
- The change is visual and should not touch inbox state, persistence, message fixtures, or compose behavior.
- Existing deployment watermark code should be preserved and kept above the UI.

## Key design decisions
- Implement the bold multi-color gradient at the app/background layer, preferably in `.app-shell`, so it appears on every app view without duplicating styles in `InboxView` or `ReaderView`.
- Preserve foreground readability by keeping message cards, reader panels, and compose panels on `neutral-surface` backgrounds with existing borders/shadows.
- Use layered CSS gradients rather than adding image assets or dependencies.
- Keep Tailwind tokens stable unless a token-level update is necessary; this minimizes risk to existing contrast tests.
- Validate with the existing workflow: `npm run format:check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and `npm run build`.
